WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:08.150
The new morning we've finally found

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:08.150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.190
is being hampered by the past.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.490
but the past so full of remorse.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.890
It's about now that a teardrop

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.810
Will this rain ever stop?

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:53.030
I've been freezing for a long time.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:53.030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:58.320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:58.320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.080
Tsutsumarete iikana

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.870
Today, the rain falls again;

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:13.090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:13.090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:18.130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:18.130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:29.850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:29.850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.340
Calm down...

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:57.260
I want to talk to you...

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.140
Please, just listen to me...

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.560
And you too, talk to me...

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.520
Yes... that's right...

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.190
You're... not alone...

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.850
Golden hair...

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.430
He must have come from the west.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.140
Well, we should at least bury him.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.900
He's alive!

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.110
You're kidding me!

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:56.900
Get yourself together!

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:57.900
Hey, are you all right?!

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.240
Water! Bring him some water!

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.290
Don't drink it in one gulp. Take it slow.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.290
Can you understand our language?

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.500
We're merchants from Xing.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.170
Where were you headed?

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.800
I have nowhere to return to...

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.970
I also have nowhere to go...

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.600
I was afraid of staying in Xerxes, so I ran...

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.440
You're right...

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.440
I'm sorry...

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.490
I couldn't stop him...

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.070
I'm sorry...!

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.780
I'm sorry, Sergence...!

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.220
The Return of the Führer

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.220
The Return of the Führer

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.470
Sergence was a master carpenter.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.260
He often came to the palace for repairs.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.180
Remember him?

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:16.020
And his son, Dozle, looked up to his father and worked hard in order to succeed him.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.610
And Caiya, the florist girl.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.150
She was kind and thoughtful.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.070
Sari, the horse owner, really loved to drink.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.870
We got along well.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.710
Little boy Tommy's dream was to become a scholar.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.080
Gidalush was a chef.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:42.260
He once got fired for giving a free meal to a traveler with no money.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.550
Andal, a fellow slave,

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:49.760
hated me for gaining the master's favor.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:55.270
Zul was a hopeless villain and was only awaiting his execution,

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.150
but he apparently wants to get back at you before that.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.730
Get back at me?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.280
Those are the souls that just infiltrated your body.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:28.590
They're cooperating with me for the sole purpose of defeating you.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.680
You're saying that the philosopher's stone is working together with you, each one retaining its own will?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.100
When they're nothing but an energy form?

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:40.650
Do you think it's impossible?

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:47.490
It almost drove me nuts to deal with these crazed souls one by one.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:52.280
But I had plenty of time to talk to them.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:56.250
Thanks to this immortal body you gave me.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.460
You talked to them?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.210
That's right.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:05.800
And that's precisely what you didn't do.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:17.270
I've already spoken to every single one of the 536329 people inside me.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.540
D-Damn you...!

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.460
Go back to where you came from,

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:45.840
Dwarf in the Flask, Homunculus.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.340
Sorry, but I'm going to be destroying your container.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.390
Tearing apart your skin is the same thing as breaking your flask.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.350
You'll turn into dust.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:08.570
Experience the will of the ones you looked down on.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:44.850
Aren't you the one who's looking down on someone, Hohenheim?

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.400
You can survive even after abandoning your skin?

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:52.450
Don't think for a moment that you fools are the only ones who progressed.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:01.160
Didn't I tell you that I'll become a perfect being?

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:13.630
What?!

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.090
A frontal attack?!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:21.350
Why must I enter my own castle through the back door?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.480
Infantry, retreat!

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.190
Impossible!

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:09.610
Did we get him?!

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.410
Take over the steering!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:19.820
Y-Yes sir!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Dammit!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.000
Where are you?!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.200
Damn you...

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.500
You took down a tank by yourself?!

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.300
Captain!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.030
Captain Buccaneer!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.740
What's the matter?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.870
The master has returned.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.910
Open the gate.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.540
Open the gate, Falman.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.380
I'm sorry, Colonel Mustang...

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.970
This may become my grave...

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:06.810
Hey, hey.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.020
Stop trying to act cool with a lame face like that.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:17.820
If it's about manliness, I can't lose to anyone either.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.530
I can still fight!

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:24.820
Rubbish.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:28.330
This is what people call 'recklessness'.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.330
Exactly.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:35.380
Letting your passions run wild and barking won't get you far at all.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.130
But for some reason...

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:44.510
I can't bring myself to abandon people like that.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:57.820
Dammit!

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:01.030
They've started to make a comeback now that the Führer President has returned!

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.780
If they get past this place, they'll take back the main gate!

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.030
Hold out no matter what!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.040
Yes.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:14.920
What?!

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.790
Are you serious?!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.920
Madam Bradley!

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.300
The Führer President is fine!

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.260
He's alive!

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.940
I'm so glad...

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.230
Are you okay?

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:43.070
Yes, I'm fine.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.150
I'm so glad...

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.070
He's alive...

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.410
Is he hurt?!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.870
I don't have the details on that yet.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:59.000
All I know is that he's wiping out the Briggs soldiers at Central Headquarters.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.840
Should we blame it on Briggs?

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:02.920
But...!

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.170
It's to protect Colonel Mustang.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:07.550
Yeah.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.890
For starters, it's great news that the Führer President is safe.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.270
Yes.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.360
I just hope Selim is safe and sound as well...

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.400
If he's fighting against the Briggs soldiers,

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:28.450
it must mean that Major General Armstrong is the mastermind behind the coup d'etat.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.200
Armstrong?

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:30.870
Oh...

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:34.330
The female general who came to Central a little while ago.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.420
Now the real problem is, how much of the upper echelon is involved?

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.130
So he was alive...

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:47.800
We can't underestimate a Homunculus, after all.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:52.390
The fact that we pretended to be on the 
Führer President's side came back to haunt us.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:56.640
We had to make Major General Armstrong out to be the villain...

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.280
This place is getting dangerous as well.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.490
Yeah.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.820
I wonder what's going to happen to us.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.620
I don't know.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.700
We've said that we're on the Führer President's side,

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.880
so I doubt they'll fire at us so easily.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.840
But what if Bradley comes back into full control again?

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:29.300
We'll probably get crushed like ants.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.050
Even if the madam is here?!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:34.180
Do you honestly think they're that compassionate?

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:45.860
It's been a while.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.610
You should have just run off somewhere after that.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.870
Unfortunately, I'm as greedy as can be.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.660
I want your life too, Wrath.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.930
Reinforcements... I'm assuming?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:18.560
Everyone in town was saying that you died in a train wreck.

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.730
How did you survive?

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.560
My eyes are too keen.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:34.780
It only takes a moment to decide the route I need to take to escape through the rubble.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.910
But I really am getting old.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.380
My body can't handle things as well as it could back then.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:48.880
He can do all this even if his body isn't at its peak?

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:54.180
Lin Yao... right?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.720
Wow!

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.850
I haven't seen you since you let me stay in your beat-up apartment!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:01.140
It's been a while, Warrant Officer Falman.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.270
I'm a Second Lieutenant now!

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.480
I owe you for a night's lodging and a meal.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.400
Let me lend you a hand.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:13.780
He said that, but both of us are actually just doing this for ourselves!

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:32.630
Trying to get into my blind spot?

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:38.930
My partner inside me taught me how to fight you.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.390
I see.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.230
Then I'll do this.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.740
He's starting to get pushed back.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.280
Isn't this looking bad for him?

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.330
Fire! Fire!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.370
Shoot!

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.590
Idiots! Don't interfere!

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:21.720
D-Damn you!!

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.020
Captain!

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.330
Seems like you have a sturdy set of abs.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:48.080
Now you won't be able to use your sword.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:50.460
Don't be reckless, moron!

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:51.170
But...!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:53.960
Good job!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.550
Christ...

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:06.180
I'm not too used to wielding these weapons.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.520
Not bad, old man.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.790
The Führer President has returned?

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:30.540
Yes, sir.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:33.790
He's currently engaged in combat with an unidentified man.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:44.720
We're going to gather more men, wipe out the small fries from Briggs,

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.930
and rescue the Führer President.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.180
Replenish weapons and fill in vacancies.

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.850
Regain the main gate.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:51.650
Yes, sir!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.360
Go! Go! Go!

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:00.780
This is bad!

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.450
The Central Soldiers have gotten back up!

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:10.620
My bad!

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.880
I've already got my hands full with him!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.540
I'm leaving the rest to you guys!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:15.920
What?!

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.840
What are we supposed to do when they have so many more men than us?!

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:22.090
Figure something out!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.720
"Figure something out"?

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.470
Captain! Hang in there!

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.430
We'll have to do just that...

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.270
Hey!

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.480
You all carry Captain Buccaneer somewhere safe!

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.400
Roger!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.730
We're going to move that.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:39.440
Roger!

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:01.300
Dammit! We're being held back by two machine guns?!

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.260
Since they have the high ground, we're at a disadvantage!

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.100
Can we get in contact with any of the squadrons in headquarters?

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.770
Have them open the gate from the inside.

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:11.600
Roger!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.100
This is the 3rd Guards Battalion!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.360
Central Headquarters Garrison, answer!

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:20.440
There are still dolls at the east gate...

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:19.860
What?

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:20.940
What are they saying?

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:22.360
Give me that.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.070
I'm Gamelan from the Guards Battalion.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.160
We're at the front gate.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.910
Can you not open the gate to headquarters from the inside?

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.290
It's impossible!

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.000
There are dolls lurking about, so we can't open the gate!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.540
Dolls?

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.170
What are you talking about?

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.430
What happened?!

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:45.680
What's going on?!

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:46.300
What?!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.090
More enemies?!

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:03.320
What on earth is going on down there?

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:30.800
Oh?

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:32.930
Not bad, gramps.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:36.940
Thanks. You saved me.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:41.440
I didn't save you. I saved the young master's body.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.190
If you say so.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:46.950
Releasing a nasty aura from the young master's body...

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:50.820
Well, I couldn't have found you otherwise.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:58.080
So, who's this guy who's left unscathed despite our combined efforts?

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:00.460
King Bradley.

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:08.970
Oh.

00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:12.430
It's my first time seeing him with my own eyes.

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:21.980
So he's the one who ripped off my granddaughter's arm...!

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:42.720
Ever since that day passed,

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:42.720
Ano hi kara zutto

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:46.970
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:46.970
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:52.520
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:52.520
Itami wo kasanetemo

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:57.630
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:57.630
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:01.070
I'll never be able

00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:01.070
Mou modorenai

00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:03.570
to return to those days.

00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:03.570
Ikutsumo no hibi

00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:08.660
I'm still powerless.

00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:08.660
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

00:23:08.660 --> 00:23:13.910
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

00:23:08.660 --> 00:23:13.910
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:19.780
memories of when you were still with me.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:19.780
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.800
I long to become

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.800
Kyou yori motto

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:25.550
stronger than I am now,

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:25.550
Tsuyoku naritai

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:30.690
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:30.690
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:33.060
If the wind happens to stop

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:33.060
Arukitsuzukete

00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:35.770
in the midst of my long journey,

00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:35.770
Kaze ga yandara

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:40.480
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:40.480
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:47.820
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:47.820
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:53.370
A rainbow spans across the sky.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:53.370
Niji ga kakaruyo

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:02.840
When a man knows the enemy, and knows himself,

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:06.540
he realizes the end of the battle.

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:09.130
However, he will not die for nothing.

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:14.970
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:19.470
Episode 57, Eternal Leave.

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:19.490
Eternal Leave

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:23.270
Farewell, my lord.

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:27.070
I shall watch over you from the other side.
